{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793353598,"nonce":"URhClrU062VCO3+cdfnTvEqJKao=","title":"Keep loaded app previews visible and recover them after session reconnect","message":"Parent: 9ef9e944325331463b0689355414f1e05696ed83ea360875764ac80432c6a239\n\nAn active landing-page preview becomes permanently blank with a build-failed message after a session connection closes. Development service refreshes reproduced this: the page removes every frame, while AppPreviewBuild clears its artifact and offers only manual Rebuild. Native preview capabilities are correctly connection-owned and revoked on disconnect; do not relax that authorization boundary.\n\nRetain the loaded frame during ordinary disconnection, reject workspace bridge calls while offline, show reconnecting feedback and automatically reacquire the preview through its existing Run Configuration and validated build caches after the same workspace reconnects. Replace the old artifact when recovery is ready; host restarts may reload the guest app. Context/account/workspace changes must remove frames and fence recovery. Closing a tab, Stop and late/cancelled worker results must not restart abandoned work or retain descriptors. No idle polling or heartbeat loop is needed: authenticated native connections have no idle timeout.\n\nVerify frame continuity while disconnected, cached reconnect without compiler processes, repeated reconnects without descriptor growth, interrupted builds, Stop/dispose and workspace replacement. Rebuild WASM and the optimized session; serve changed browser assets without restarting an unchanged session service.","files":null}]}